# Penpixel Creative: security headers (Cloudflare Pages)
# Reviewed against OWASP Top 10 (2021): A05 (misconfiguration), A02 (transport).

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://www.googletagmanager.com 'sha256-oJviho+4/VcFLOKyHzqua2Zs/Np50hZoQwtIcJak5as='; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data: https://www.google-analytics.com; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://www.google-analytics.com https://*.google-analytics.com; frame-src https://challenges.cloudflare.com; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), browsing-topics=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin

# Long-cache fingerprinted build assets
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CSP NOTE (Turnstile): script-src + frame-src include challenges.cloudflare.com
# The documented minimum for the Turnstile bot-protection widget on /contact.
# connect-src stays 'self' (siteverify happens server-side in the Pages Function).
#
# CSP NOTE: style-src is 'self' (no 'unsafe-inline') because the build emits
# zero inline styles: Tailwind utilities only, no scoped <style> blocks, and
# astro.config sets build.inlineStylesheets:'never'. If you later add a scoped
# <style> in a component, Astro will inline it and this CSP will block it.
# Fix then by enabling Astro's experimental CSP (auto-hashes styles) rather
# than re-adding 'unsafe-inline'.
#
# CSP NOTE (GA4 / gtag.js, src/components/GoogleAnalytics.astro):
# script-src allows googletagmanager.com for the external gtag.js loader,
# plus a SHA-256 hash for the small inline bootstrap script instead of
# 'unsafe-inline'. That hash is computed on the EXACT bytes Astro renders
# between <script> and </script> for that one component. If you ever edit
# GoogleAnalytics.astro's inline script -- even whitespace -- run
# `npm run build` and recompute the hash (see script below) or GA breaks
# silently: CSP fails closed, no console error a visitor would notice,
# tracking just stops firing.
#   node -e "
#     const fs=require('fs'),c=require('crypto');
#     const html=fs.readFileSync('dist/index.html','utf8');
#     const m=[...html.matchAll(/<script>(.*?)<\/script>/gs)].find(x=>x[1].includes('gaId'));
#     console.log('sha256-'+c.createHash('sha256').update(m[1]).digest('base64'));
#   "
# connect-src / img-src allow google-analytics.com (+ wildcard subdomain for
# GA4's regional collection endpoints, e.g. region1.google-analytics.com).
# No SRI on the gtag.js loader: Google doesn't publish stable per-version
# file hashes for it (same accepted tradeoff as the Turnstile loader above).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
